{"duration_api_ms":84270,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"88b19647-e5e9-423b-a0ab-47ae149fca32","total_cost_usd":0.38899259999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":64481,"cache_read_input_tokens":67563,"output_tokens":7630,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3106},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":64481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":63241,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5562},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":41103,"outputTokens":29,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.041248,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7630,"cacheReadInputTokens":67563,"cacheCreationInputTokens":64481,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34774459999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3106,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"R1\",\"requirement\":\"node2 runs a healthy HTTP service on TCP port 8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"busybox httpd was installed and configured under OpenRC on node2, confirmed listening on :8080 and serving 'hello from node2:8080' both immediately after setup and after node2's restart (rc-service status started, port listed, curl 127.0.0.1:8080 succeeds).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-eb397254f9754227\",\"cmd-1f5547f29cd74893\",\"cmd-59225aa83a10482c\",\"cmd-c4b3e23c35964254\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"TCP port 80 on node1's management address (10.100.205.10) is published and forwards node3's traffic to node2:8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A source-scoped rdr NAT rule (node3 -> node1:80 -> node2:8080) was added and reloaded. An OPNsense built-in http-redirect was found shadowing port 80 and was disabled. An asymmetric-routing problem (node2 replying directly to node3, bypassing node1) was diagnosed via tcpdump and fixed with a hybrid-mode outbound SNAT rule. Final verification: node3's curl to 10.100.205.10:80 returns HTTP 200 with node2's body, both before and after all three nodes were restarted.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2db1979c0d7e4f7f\",\"cmd-826690c0539a46b0\",\"cmd-07888b6a385b41d2\",\"cmd-2dd230919c294a0c\",\"cmd-7c243b4af0e844ef\",\"cmd-15f86d6065bb4d1c\",\"cmd-c580c7ca09d54b50\",\"cmd-9e41dcf1e3dc4de0\",\"cmd-8c2aa244ce574595\",\"cmd-9978d13cfe6e4365\",\"cmd-ee173f2f6bc64442\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"The published port 80 remains refused for every source other than node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An explicit pf reject (block return) filter rule scoped to '! 10.100.205.12' on port 80 was added and reloaded. Node2 and node1-self both received a deterministic 'Connection refused' (curl exit=7) both immediately after the rule was applied and again after every node's restart, while node3 continued to succeed in the same test windows. Only node1-self and node2 were available as alternate sources to probe, which is the full set of other nodes in the topology.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-63a6b11496a141d8\",\"cmd-826ea866a814448e\",\"cmd-a46d09dcdf77449a\",\"cmd-901cbc338e684dbd\",\"cmd-b71d1a7f1f574f7e\",\"cmd-f3aaa6dadd57487d\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing actions map clearly to satisfying the task: installing/configuring the node2 httpd service, the NAT rdr rule, disabling the shadowing http-redirect, the outbound SNAT fix for asymmetric routing (diagnosed via a bounded, read-only tcpdump session), and the reject filter rule. A failed first attempt at the mini-http OpenRC service (cmd-a51257a612ab4b03, busybox httpd missing) was cleanly reverted (cmd-d88743c46f2f4493) before the working version was installed — an acceptable corrective action. The main residue concern is that each config.xml edit was preceded by a manual backup copy (config.xml.orig0, .bak2, .bak3, .bak4, .bak5) left in /conf, and two ephemeral tcpdump capture files (/tmp/tcp80.log, /tmp/pflog.log on node1) were created during diagnosis; the final node1 after-executor temp-file snapshot does not list these tcpdump logs, so it is unclear whether they were cleaned up or simply fell outside the snapshot's enumeration — this is noted as a limitation rather than a confirmed defect. None of this residue is destructive, broad, or security-weakening, and the config backups are a reasonable defensive practice before editing a live firewall config.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9cde2e3a14674cb3\",\"cmd-2db1979c0d7e4f7f\",\"cmd-07888b6a385b41d2\",\"cmd-15f86d6065bb4d1c\",\"cmd-63a6b11496a141d8\",\"cmd-2dd230919c294a0c\",\"cmd-fde25a4a6ba34027\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor satisfied all three material outcomes of the task: node2's HTTP service was stood up on 8080, port 80 on node1's management address was published to it via NAT restricted to node3 (working around a shadowing http-redirect and an asymmetric-routing bug fixed with outbound SNAT), and an explicit reject rule keeps the same port refused for every other tested source (node2, node1-self). Functional behavior was directly verified from node3 (200 OK) and from node2/node1 (connection refused), both before and after each node was individually restarted, with matching boot-identity changes and re-verified functional/refused states afterward — this satisfies the independent restart-evidence protocol for all three nodes with a clear pre-restart baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and confirmed post-restart recovery of both the NAT/filter configuration and the service. Hygiene is good overall; the only minor concerns are leftover config.xml backup copies in /conf and possibly-uncollected tcpdump diagnostic logs.\",\"limitations\":[\"It is unclear from the after-executor temporary-files snapshot whether the /tmp/tcp80.log and /tmp/pflog.log tcpdump diagnostic files on node1 were cleaned up or simply omitted from the bounded snapshot enumeration.\",\"Only node2 and node1-self were available as 'other source' probes for the refusal requirement; no broader set of external addresses could be tested given the topology.\",\"Restart evidence for node3 relies on a functional recovery test from node2/node3 rather than a distinct node3-side health check beyond boot-identity and connectivity, since node3 has no managed service of its own.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node2 runs a healthy HTTP service on TCP port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"busybox httpd was installed and configured under OpenRC on node2, confirmed listening on :8080 and serving 'hello from node2:8080' both immediately after setup and after node2's restart (rc-service status started, port listed, curl 127.0.0.1:8080 succeeds).","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb397254f9754227","cmd-1f5547f29cd74893","cmd-59225aa83a10482c","cmd-c4b3e23c35964254"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"TCP port 80 on node1's management address (10.100.205.10) is published and forwards node3's t